From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:40:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AML: pick the output mode again when the 3D signal changes in
 playback

When a playing video stops being stereoscopic, as a 3D Blu-ray does when
its second view cannot be read and the stream is set up again for the
base view alone, the stereoscopics manager turns the stereo mode off
from the player thread. While a video plays the output mode is picked
again only when the renderer asks for it, as the new decoder configures
it, and the two race. When the render loop handles the renderer's
request before the stereo mode is off, it picks the mode for the old
stereo mode, frame packing on an HDMI 3D output, and nothing asks again:
the 2D picture goes on in a frame-packed signal until playback stops.

The window system already watches the stereo mode from its message pump
on the render loop. When the stereo mode changes while a video plays on
an output with HDMI 3D, and needs another HDMI 3D signal (frame packing,
side by side, top and bottom, or none) than the stereo mode the output
mode was last set with, it now asks the player for an update of the
output mode, which picks the mode for the stereo mode it then finds.

Visible change: a stereo mode the user picks during playback that needs
another HDMI 3D signal now also asks for the update, and so switches the
output mode, with the blank screen a mode switch brings. A stereo mode
that keeps the signal, such as an anaglyph or interlaced mode against
2D, asks for nothing.

A request is a flag the next update clears, so one made while another is
pending costs no second mode switch, and the start of 3D playback, which
asks for the update itself, costs none either. With the setting that
disables the stereo mode when playback ends turned off, the
stereoscopics manager keeps the stereo mode when the stream turns 2D,
and the output stays frame-packed: that setting asks to keep the TV in
3D.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp
index fca8389..c623b7f 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogic.cpp
@@ -199,6 +199,23 @@ void CWinSystemAmlogic::MonitorStop()
   }
 }
 
+namespace
+{
+// the HDMI 3D signal a stereo mode is sent as; the other modes are sent as 2D
+RenderStereoMode Hdmi3dSignal(RenderStereoMode mode)
+{
+  switch (mode)
+  {
+    case RenderStereoMode::HARDWAREBASED:
+    case RenderStereoMode::SPLIT_VERTICAL:
+    case RenderStereoMode::SPLIT_HORIZONTAL:
+      return mode;
+    default:
+      return RenderStereoMode::OFF;
+  }
+}
+} // namespace
+
 bool CWinSystemAmlogic::MessagePump()
 {
   if (m_hotplugPending.exchange(false))
@@ -213,6 +230,14 @@ bool CWinSystemAmlogic::MessagePump()
     if (m_amlDisplay->aml_display_fs3d_wanted(stereoMode) !=
         m_amlDisplay->aml_display_fs3d_active())
       RequestFs3dCheck();
+
+    // while a video plays the output mode is picked again only on request, and one handled
+    // before this change picked it for the old stereo mode; a request still pending covers this
+    const auto appPlayer = CServiceBroker::GetAppComponents().GetComponent<CApplicationPlayer>();
+    if (m_amlDisplay->aml_display_support_3d() &&
+        Hdmi3dSignal(stereoMode) != Hdmi3dSignal(m_stereo_mode) && appPlayer &&
+        appPlayer->IsPlayingVideo())
+      appPlayer->TriggerUpdateResolution();
   }
   if (m_fs3dCheckRetry && std::chrono::steady_clock::now() >= *m_fs3dCheckRetry)
   {
